            <fr:title text="Lemma V">Lemma V</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>lemma</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">refuted</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">result13_addendum.md; certificates p5_vtprime (EQUALITY), p5_lemmaV_asym; p5_vt_check's "FAILURES" line reports the superseded condition only.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Lemma V, as originally stated: for a split
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_L, v, c_R)]]></fr:tex> with reductive quotient data
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) \le  z_u(c') + v^2.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> <html:strong>False as stated</html:strong> over all splits: 958 counterexample
splits in umod_tables.tsv at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  12]]></fr:tex>. The smallest is
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (1,2,3,1)]]></fr:tex> split as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(1) \mid  (2) \mid  (3,1)]]></fr:tex>, where
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[11 > 6 + 4]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>Two regimes survive and are proven. All 3-block splits <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(a, v, b)]]></fr:tex> —
H17<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>, five sub-lemmas: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sigma ]]></fr:tex>-avoidance (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) giving
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  K \le  z']]></fr:tex> with equality; the decomposition
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K = x_{XY} \oplus  K_0]]></fr:tex>; and a quotient-restriction injection into
intertwiners whose kernel is killed by the
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {v}{2} + \binom {v}{2}]]></fr:tex> against <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v^2]]></fr:tex> count, with
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\text {intw} = \binom {|a-b|}{2}]]></fr:tex>. And the tall regime,
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> The old condition (V-t) <html:em>fails</html:em> when <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[|a - b| \ge  2]]></fr:tex>, at
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {|a-b|}{2}]]></fr:tex>; (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is its repair. (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is itself false
in the multi-block setting, and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {V}_0 \le  v^2]]></fr:tex> holds only for
the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathfrak {k}]]></fr:tex>-version.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Superseded by:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link> for the tall regime; <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:link> for the
general case.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>.</html:p>
